  "text": "That's every puzzle. Two definitions left. Covariance tracks how two variables move together, but its size depends on their units: the same people give forty-two in centimeters and point four two in meters. Correlation divides by both standard deviations, so it stays between minus one and one. And zero correlation rules out a straight line, not a relationship. Last, the expected value of a bet that pays ten dollars one time in five, and loses three otherwise. Two dollars, minus two forty: it loses forty cents a play, though its likeliest outcome is losing three. A model's output is a probability too. The next round asks whether it holds up on data the model hasn't seen, and how you'd score it. Next: machine learning, training and evaluating.",
